Description: Provides lightweight, version-aware access to the annotation
    resources used by SpaMTP. Resources include pruned RaMP chemical,
    identifier, pathway, and pathway-topology tables, precomputed SMILES
    functional-group and ionisation features, and legacy metabolite reference
    tables, plus a separately versioned human gene identifier reference from
    fixed HGNC archives. RaMP resource files are hosted on Zenodo and described
    by AnnotationHub metadata rather than bundled in the package. Retrieved files are
    verified against recorded sizes and checksums and cached for reuse, and a
    local resource directory can be used for development and reproducible
    database builds. Maintainer recipes coordinate a shared Zenodo resource
    collection with SpaMTPData while preserving separate annotation and
    experiment registries and independent resource versions.
